[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Open Games (1...e5)"]
[Variation "Four Knights Game: Spanish Variation"]
[ECO "C48"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "fork"]
[Themes "pin-the-knight,symmetry"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "3.Nc3"]
[Start "giuoco-piano 2...Nc6"]

3. Nc3 { White develops and defends e4. } 3... Nf6 { Mirrors White: the knight develops and attacks e4. } 4. Bb5 ( 4. d3 d5 { White's quiet move gives Black time to strike in the centre at once. } 5. exd5 Nxd5 ) ( 4. d4 exd4 5. Nxd4 Bb4 { Pins the knight on c3 to the king, so it cannot support the centre. } 6. Nxc6 bxc6 7. Bd3 ( 7. Bd2 O-O 8. Bd3 d5 ) 7... d5 { Strikes in the centre and opens lines for Black's pieces. } 8. exd5 cxd5 9. O-O O-O ) ( 4. Bc4 Nxe4 { The fork trick: Black takes e4 because ...d5 will fork the bishop and the knight. } 5. Nxe4 d5 { The pawn forks the bishop on c4 and the knight on e4, so Black wins one piece back. } 6. Bd3 dxe4 7. Bxe4 Bd6 { Develops with a plan to castle. The position is level. } ) 4... Bb4 { Attacks the knight that guards e4, the same idea White just used against c6. } 5. O-O ( 5. Bxc6 dxc6 6. Nxe5 Bxc3 7. dxc3 Qxd1+ 8. Kxd1 Nxe4 { Black wins the pawn back, and the endgame is level. } ) ( 5. d3 d6 ) ( 5. a3 Bxc3 6. dxc3 Nxe4 { With the knight on c3 gone, e4 has no defender. } ) 5... O-O { Castle: the king is safe and the rook joins the centre. } 6. d3 d6 { Gives e5 a pawn defender, so the knight on c6 no longer has to guard it, and opens the bishop on c8. } 7. Bg5 Bxc3 { Trades the pinning bishop for the knight and gives White doubled pawns on the c-file. } 8. bxc3 Qe7 { Steps out of the pin: the bishop on g5 can no longer pin the knight on f6 to the queen. } 9. Re1 a6 { Asks the bishop on b5 what it wants. } 10. Ba4 h6 { Asks the bishop on g5 what it wants, with a good reply to either. Plan: ...Nd8-e6 and ...c5. White's doubled pawns on the c-file are a long-term weakness. } *
